INT. SWIFTLINE DELIVERY WAREHOUSE - MORNING

We see a huge warehouse with many shelves and conveyor belts. Its early morning and the lights are still turning on one by one. BARRY, 40s, a shift supervisor who thinks he is very important, walks in carrying a coffee and a clipboard.

CLOSE ON Barry's name tag, which says "BARRY - SUPERVISOR" in big letters.

BARRY
Good morning team! Big day today!

Nobody answers. We see NADINE, 30s, tired, sitting on a pallet jack eating a granola bar, and ROBIN, 20s, who uses they/them pronouns, scrolling on their phone near the sorting belt.

NADINE
Its 6 AM Barry.

BARRY
And whats that mean? It means the early bird gets the worm!

ROBIN
(muttering to self)
I dont even like worms.

BARRY
What was that Robin?

ROBIN
Nothing. Good morning.

Barry nods happily and puts his coffee down on a stack of boxes marked FRAGILE, then walks to the control panel and presses a green button and the belt starts to move slowly, and Nadine stands up and stretches while Robin puts their phone in their pocket and walks to the end of the belt and picks up the first package, and Barry checks his clipboard and looks very pleased with himself while a forklift beeps somewhere far away.

BARRY
(to everyone)
Okay everybody listen up. Today is a normal day. Nothing special. Just normal packages, normal routes, normal everything.

NADINE
You said normal three times.

BARRY
Because its normal!

Nadine looks at Robin. Robin looks at Nadine. They both look at Barry.

ROBIN
(quietly, to Nadine)
He's lying about something.

NADINE
(quietly)
Obviously.

We see the belt carry a small brown box down the line. It is the only box that is not scanned by the machine. CLOSE ON the box. It has a red sticker that says "DO NOT OPEN - PRIVATE".

NADINE (CONT'D)
(reading the label)
Barry what is this?

BARRY
(too fast)
Its nothing. Just a regular box. Put it back.

ROBIN
It doesnt have a barcode.

BARRY
Some boxes dont have barcodes Robin that is a known thing.

Robin lifts the box off the belt. It is light. Something inside RATTLES softly. Barry's face goes white and he drops his clipboard, which CLATTERS on the concrete floor.

NADINE
(to herself)
Oh no. He's sweating.

BARRY
Please put it down. Please. Both of you.

ROBIN
(to the room)
Is it a bomb?

BARRY
Its not a bomb!

NADINE
Then open it.

BARRY
I cant let you open it!

Nadine takes the box from Robin and in one move she tears the red sticker and rips the tape. Robin leans in, Barry covers his eyes with both hands, and a forklift driver in the distance honks twice for no reason.

CLOSE ON the open box. Inside are forty-two tiny bottles of hotel shampoo, six stolen name tags from other supervisors, and a laminated sign that says "WORLDS BEST BOSS".

Silence.

NADINE
These are the name tags from Dayton.

ROBIN
Barry. Did you make yourself an award?

BARRY
(small voice)
It was going to be a surprise.

NADINE
For who?

BARRY
For me. At the Friday meeting. I was going to have you all give it to me.

ROBIN
(to Nadine)
I want to be mad but I'm mostly impressed.

NADINE
(to the group of the whole warehouse, shouting)
Hey everybody! Barry made himself an award!

From far away in the building we hear a slow, growing round of applause, and a lone forklift honks. Barry sits down on the pallet jack and puts his face in his hands.

BARRY
(muffled)
Can I at least keep the shampoo.

Nadine tosses him one small bottle. Robin sets the laminated sign on top of Barry's head like a crown.

ROBIN
Congratulations boss.
